{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 19, :comments ["<b>You shall not let mate כל</b> — אים. And juxtaposed to it: ואיש כי ישכב את אשה — ש\"ז, and she is a שפחה נרחפת, which is like כלאים, for she is half slave and half free. And juxtaposed to שפחה חרופה: ערלתו את פריו — to say that one who lies with a שפחה חרופה, the פרי will be wicked. And further, as we say: נטיע' מקטע רגליהון דבועלי נדות — like this one who could not wait until she was freed."], :book :leviticus, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 19, :notes {0 "The word אים after כל appears to be a Masorah or textual notation; rendered as found. ש\"ז likely indicates a numerical or mnemonic notation. The Aramaic phrases נטיע' מקטע רגליהון דבועלי נדות are left in Hebrew script per discipline."}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-12T19:20:04.787254252Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}